  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Joint Partnership between UNFPA and IOM for Cash Assistance to Pregnant and Lactating Women</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More than 15 months after the large-scale Russian invasion of Ukraine, it is estimated that more than 5.4 million people displaced in the country &#x2013; 58 per cent of whom displaced for six months or more and 5.6 million returnees. Conflict continues to increase the humanitarian crisis and has led to a multitude of stressors and challenges that are often difficult for people affected by the war to cope with. The need for immediate assistance is immense especially for pregnant and lactating women in Ukraine considering their additional needs. 
 
Through one-time cash assistance to 5,200 lactating and pregnant women, and in partnership with the United Nations Population Fund, the International Organization for Migration is contributing towards the mitigation of negative effects of the war on pregnant and lactating women in Ukraine, reducing their vulnerabilities and addressing their needs.</narrative>
  </description>
